From 8cc6a30fb1a52e62b88804abf2f1b4555a399bfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 08:33:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add auto-contrast typewriter label to floating contact button

Adds a looping "Contact Us" label beside the floating contact icon on
every page. The label uses mix-blend-mode: difference so its text
color automatically inverts against whatever section is behind it
(white on dark backgrounds, black on light ones), with a steps()
typewriter animation that types and retypes on a loop.

The label is a standalone fixed element (a sibling of .floating-actions,
not nested inside it) because .floating-actions already establishes its
own stacking context via position: fixed + z-index, which would have
confined the blend to within that context instead of the real page
behind it. The scroll-to-top and contact buttons are also reordered so
the contact button's position stays fixed regardless of whether the
scroll-to-top button is currently shown, keeping the label aligned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SjcntVjf5Nr2bdomgFdfPu
